{
 "formato": "sktch",
 "versao": 1,
 "gerado": "demo do CircuitSketch",
 "codigo": [
  "// Blue Pill: the onboard LED and a button.",
  "//",
  "// Two things that catch people coming to the STM32 from the Arduino:",
  "//",
  "//  1. The pin is not called \"13\" but PC13. In the Arduino core",
  "//     for STM32 the ports are numbered in sequence, and PC13",
  "//     becomes 45 -- which is what LED_BUILTIN is here.",
  "//  2. The onboard LED lights with LOW, not HIGH.",
  "",
  "const int BUTTON = 16;   // PB0",
  "",
  "void setup() {",
  "  Serial.begin(115200);",
  "  pinMode(LED_BUILTIN, OUTPUT);",
  "  pinMode(BUTTON, INPUT_PULLUP);",
  "}",
  "",
  "void loop() {",
  "  bool pressed = digitalRead(BUTTON) == LOW;",
  "",
  "  // Inverted on purpose: on the Blue Pill the LED lights on LOW.",
  "  digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, pressed ? LOW : HIGH);",
  "",
  "  Serial.println(pressed ? \"pressed\" : \"released\");",
  "  delay(200);",
  "}"
 ],
 "circuito": {
  "Pecas": [
   {
    "Id": "bb",
    "Tipo": "protoboard-830",
    "X": 40,
    "Y": 260
   },
   {
    "Id": "placa",
    "Tipo": "stm32-bluepill",
    "X": 70,
    "Y": 30
   },
   {
    "Id": "bt",
    "Tipo": "pushbutton",
    "X": 320,
    "Y": 300
   }
  ],
  "Fios": [
   {
    "DePeca": "placa",
    "DePino": "PB0",
    "ParaPeca": "bt",
    "ParaPino": "1.l",
    "Cor": "#2E6BD0",
    "Estilo": "solto"
   },
   {
    "DePeca": "bt",
    "DePino": "2.l",
    "ParaPeca": "placa",
    "ParaPino": "GND.2",
    "Cor": "#111111",
    "Estilo": "solto"
   }
  ]
 },
 "descricao": [
  "STM32F103 \"Blue Pill\" with the onboard LED and a button.",
  "",
  "What this example shows:",
  "",
  "1. On the STM32 a pin is named after its port: PC13, PB0, PA5. The Arduino core numbers them in sequence (PA0..PA15 = 0..15, PB0 = 16, PC13 = 45), and that number is what digitalWrite takes.",
  "2. The onboard LED lights with LOW. That is why the code writes the inverted value -- and why everyone thinks the board came dead the first time.",
  "",
  "Press F5 and hold the button."
 ]
}